{
  // Typecheck-only config for everything the build config cannot see.
  //
  // `tsconfig.json` is the BUILD config: `rootDir: "./src"` and
  // `include: ["src/**/*"]`, because dev scripts and tests must not be compiled
  // into build/ or shipped in the .mcpb. The side effect was that
  // `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` exited 0 no matter what `dev/` or `tests/`
  // contained — it never opened those files. So the check that covers them has
  // to be a separate project with `noEmit`. Run via `npm run typecheck`, which
  // `pretest` invokes so it cannot be forgotten.
  //
  // TWO incidents motivate this, found independently and worth keeping both:
  //
  //   1. (#1328) A broken edit to the ~5,000-line qualifier probe — a reference
  //      to an identifier declared inside a different section's function —
  //      passed a "typecheck clean" check that had never looked at it, and
  //      would have thrown at runtime after several minutes of live API calls.
  //
  //   2. (#1324) Widening `findRepresentedPerson`'s return type broke a test at
  //      runtime while `tsc` stayed green, because `tests/` was never in scope.
  //
  // Incident 1 argues for `dev/`; incident 2 argues for `tests/`. One config
  // covering `src` + `dev` + `tests` answers both. It supersedes the narrower
  // `tsconfig.dev.json` + `typecheck:dev` pair (#1328), which covered `dev/`
  // only — deleted rather than kept alongside, because two overlapping
  // typecheck projects with `pretest` running one of them is how someone gets a
  // green check that never opened their files, which is incident 1 again.
  //
  // `tests/` was deliberately excluded when #1328 wrote its version, for a good
  // reason at the time: vitest transpiles without typechecking, so the suite had
  // never been type-clean, and including it surfaced 126 pre-existing errors
  // (assertions reading a union they had not discriminated) which — since
  // `pretest` runs this — would have blocked `npm test` repo-wide until every
  // one was fixed. That precondition is gone: all 126 were fixed in #1324, so
  // the exclusion is no longer load-bearing.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "declaration": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "dev/**/*", "tests/**/*"]

  // No `exclude`, deliberately. This landed with 13 files carved out carrying
  // those 126 errors; all were fixed and the list is gone. Do not reintroduce
  // one to get a red check green — fix the types.
}
